
	Prosody FMP processing
secname	sort
	Create a FMP[rx] endpoint
apifn	sm_fmprx_create
params	sm_fmprx_create_parms fmprxp
	The newly created FMP[rx].
field	tSMFMPrxId fmprx out
	A value obtained from
fnref	sm_open_module
	which indicates the module where the FMP[rx] is to be allocated.
field	tSMModuleId module in
enumstart	kSMFMPrxType
	The FMP[rx] is to receive IPv4 packets
enum	kSMFMPrxTypeIPv4
	The FMP[rx] is to receive IPv6 packets
enum	kSMFMPrxTypeIPv6
enumend	type in
	The address on which this FMP[rx] is to listen if
ref	type
	is 
ref	kSMFMPrxTypeIPv4.
field	in_addr address in
	The address on which this FMP[rx] is to listen if
ref	type
	is 
ref	kSMFMPrxTypeIPv6.
field	in6_addr ipv6_address in
unstruct
	Allocates, on a specific module, a new FMP[rx] to receive incoming T.38 data.
	If the call completes successfully, the parameter
ref	fmprx
	will be set to the identifier for that fmprx.
	<p>
	A FMP[rx] is automatically allocated a port number for incoming
	RTP data, this information may be obtained by waiting for
fnref	sm_fmprx_status
	to return the port information.
	The FMP[rx] will discard any incoming packets that do not match it's
	current configuration settings.
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  fmprx
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error	ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - if insufficient resources exist to create the FMP[rx]

	Destroy a previously allocated FMP[rx]
apifn	sm_fmprx_destroy
	A tSMFMPrxId that has been prevously created by a call to 
fnref	sm_fmprx_create.
param	tSMFMPrxId fmprx
	Destroys
ref	fmprx
	and invalidates the tSMFMPrxId.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Obtain a data feed from a FMP[rx]
apifn	sm_fmprx_get_datafeed
params	sm_fmprx_datafeed_parms datafeedp
	The fmp[rx] from which to obtain a datafeed
field	tSMFMPrxId fmprx in
	The datafeed object associated with the FMP[rx]
field   tSMDatafeedId datafeed out
unstruct
	Request a datafeed identifier from a FMP[rx]. This identifer can 
	subsequently be used in a call to 
fnref	sm_channel_datafeed_connect
	or
fnref	sm_fmptx_datafeed_connect
	to connect a FMP[rx] to a speech channel (tSMChannelId) or a FMP[tx]
	respectively. Datafeed connections can only be made between objects
	allocated on the same <code>tSMModuleId</code>.
	<p>
	Requires the modules
modref  datafeed
modref  fmprx
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Obtain an event for a FMP[rx]
apifn	sm_fmprx_get_event
params	sm_fmprx_event_parms eventp
	The FMP[rx] 
field	tSMFMPrxId fmprx in
	The event identifier
field	tSMEventId event out
unstruct
	If the call completes successfully 
ref	event
	will hold a pointer to the tSMEventId belonging to 
ref	fmprx.
	The tSMEventId is valid until the FMP[rx] is destroyed using 
fnref	sm_fmprx_destroy.
	This event will be signalled when a status change occurs on the FMP[rx].
	When the event is signalled the user must call 
fnref	sm_fmprx_status
	to discover the nature of the status change.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Determine FMP[rx] status
apifn	sm_fmprx_status
params	sm_fmprx_status_parms statusp
	The FMP[rx] to interrogate
field	tSMFMPrxId fmprx in
enumstart kSMFMPrxStatus
	Indicates that there is nothing significant to report
enum	kSMFMPrxStatusRunning
	Indicates that the FMP[rx] has stopped processing T.38 and that
	it can be safely destroyed
enum	kSMFMPrxStatusStopped
	Indicates that IPv4 port information is available.
enum	kSMFMPrxStatusGotPorts
	Indicates that IPv4 source address and port information is available.
enum	kSMFMPrxStatusSource
	Indicates that IPv6 port information is available.
enum	kSMFMPrxStatusGotPortsIPv6
	Indicates that IPv6 source address and port information is available.
enum	kSMFMPrxStatusSourceIPv6
enumend status out
union
	This field is only valid if the status is
ref	kSMFMPrxStatusGotPorts.
struct
	The UDP port number on which this FMP[rx] is listening for T.38 packets
field	int T38_port out
	The IPv4 address on which this FMP[rx] is listening
field	in_addr address out
unstruct	port
	This field is only valid if the status is
ref	kSMFMPrxStatusSource.
struct
	The IPv4 address from which the T.38 data is being received.
field	in_addr address out
	The UDP port number from which the T.38 data is being received.
field	int port out
unstruct	source
	This field is only valid if the status is
ref	kSMFMPrxStatusGotPortsIPv6.
struct
	The UDP port number on which this FMP[rx] is listening for T.38 packets
field	int T38_port out
	The IPv6 address on which this FMP[rx] is listening
field	in6_addr address out
unstruct	port_ipv6
	This field is only valid if the status is
ref	kSMFMPrxStatusSourceIPv6.
struct
	The IPv6 address from which the T.38 data is being received.
field	in6_addr address out
	The UDP port number from which the T.38 data is being received.
field	int port out
unstruct	source_ipv6
unstruct	u
unstruct
	Returns the current status of the FMP[rx] or an error to indicate that
	an error has occurred.
	<p>
	When the event, obtained from
fnref	sm_fmprx_get_event,
	is signalled the user must call this function to determine the nature of
	the status change. The change in status may indicate that an error occurred
	whilst processing a user request or it may be notifiying the user of a
	change to the previous state of the FMP[rx].
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error	ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - if insufficient resources existed to create the FMP[rx]

	Instructs a FMP[rx] to stop processing T.38
apifn	sm_fmprx_stop
params	sm_fmprx_stop_parms stopp
	A tSMFMPrxId that has been previously created by a call to
fnref	sm_fmprx_create.
field	tSMFMPrxId fmprx in
unstruct
	Requests that a FMP[rx] stops executing. The user will be notified that
	a FMP[rx] has terminated by a final status event. Once the final status
	notification has been received the FMP[rx] can be destroyed using
fnref	sm_fmprx_destroy.
	<p>
	Once the FMP[rx] has stopped the event should no longer be used to wait
	for status notifications as it will be signalled permanently. The event
	is invalidated when
fnref	sm_fmprx_destroy
	is called.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Configure the basic options for FMP[tx] to use IPv4
apifn	sm_fmptx_config
params	sm_fmptx_config_parms configp
	The FMP[tx] to configure
field	tSMFMPtxId fmptx in
	The SOCKADDR_IN structure specifying the destination IP address
	and port for the T38 data. A struct SOCKADDR_IN must be
	configured with an address family, an IP address and a port.
	Note that most operating systems define this structure such that
	fields are in network byte order.
	The structure must be correctly cast such that an IP V4 
	address is specified.
field	SOCKADDR_IN destination in
	The SOCKADDR_IN structure allows you to specify the source IP
	address and port for the T.38 data. A struct SOCKADDR_IN must
	be configured with an address family. The IP address may be
	specified, or the value INADDR_ANY may be used to indicate
	that any suitable address may be used. The port number may be
	specified, or the value zero may be used to indicate that a
	suitable port number is to be automatically allocated and
	used.
	Note that most operating systems define this structure such that
	fields are in network byte order.
	The structure must be correctly cast such that an IP V4 
	address is specified.
field	SOCKADDR_IN source in
	The type of error protection to use
enumstart kSMFMPRecoveryType
	Indicates that Redundancy is to be used
enum	kSMFMPRecoveryTypeRED
	Indicates that Forward Error Correction is to be used, (not
	currently supported)
enum	kSMFMPRecoveryTypeFEC
	Indicates the Redundancy over RTP is to be used, (not currently
	supported)
enum	kSMFMPRecoveryTypeRTP
enumend	Recovery in
	Indicates the level of Redundancy to apply to packets. This is the
	number of secondaries to include in each packet.
field	tSM_UT32 RecoveryLevel in
unstruct
	Configures a FMP[tx] to send T.38 data to a device with the 
	specified IPv4 address.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

