	Create a FMP[tx] endpoint
apifn	sm_fmptx_create
params	sm_fmptx_create_parms fmptxp
	The newly created FMP[tx].
field	tSMFMPtxId fmptx out
	A value obtained from
fnref	sm_open_module
	which indicates the module where the FMP[tx] is to be allocated.
field	tSMModuleId module in
unstruct
	Allocates, on a specific module, a new FMP[tx] to transmit T.38 data to a 
	remote device.
	<p>
	If the call completes successfully, the parameter
ref	fmptx
	will be set to the identifier for that FMP[tx].
	<p>
	Requires the module
modref  fmptx
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error	ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - if insufficient resources exist to create the FMP[tx]

	Connect a datafeed to an FMP[tx]
apifn	sm_fmptx_datafeed_connect
params	sm_fmptx_datafeed_connect_parms datafeedp
	The datafeed acting as a source of data
field   tSMDatafeedId data_source in
	The FMP[tx] that will receive the data
field	tSMFMPtxId data_dest in
unstruct
	Connects a datafeed to a FMP[tx]. The
ref	data_source
	must be a datafeed obtained from 
fnref	sm_channel_get_datafeed
	or 
fnref	sm_fmprx_get_datafeed.
	The channel 
ref	data_dest
	will recieve any data that is generated by the output task from which 
ref	data_source
	was derived.
	<p> To disconnect a FMP[tx] from a datafeed, specify 
	<code>kSMNullDatafeedId</code> as the tSMDatafeedId in
ref	data_source.
	<p>
	Requires the modules
modref  datafeed
modref  fmptx
	to have been downloaded.
explain
	0
retval

